Review for **PR 1522** at head `3395325122ef0bac8e49f82c08606f706ff48444` is posted as **MODIFY** on the eval gate (`post_verdict` returned `posted: true`). This session has **no code runner** (`Shell`/`Bash` unavailable; `compare_suite_runs` → `eval-no-runner`), so the pinned wall-clock budget could not be **measured** here—only structural analysis below.

### JWT pattern change

**Base (diff):** `\beyJ…{8,}\.…{8,}\.…{8,}\b` — unbounded segments.

**Head:** `(?<![A-Za-z0-9_])eyJ[A-Za-z0-9_-]{8,2048}\.[A-Za-z0-9_-]{8,2048}\.[A-Za-z0-9_-]{8,2048}\b` — bounded segments and a fixed left edge instead of `\b`.

**Consumer (inferred):** `redactSecrets` runs this in the `VALUE_PATTERNS` loop after assignment scrub and URL userinfo scrub.

### Pinned input: `eyJ-` × 50,000 → 200,000 chars, no dots

| Budget part | **inferred** behavior | Meets pin? |
| --- | --- | --- |
| **(1) N vs 2N (time at 2N ≤ 3× time at N)** | On a run with no `.`, each `(?<![A-Za-z0-9_])eyJ` attempt fails at the required dot after at most **2048** first-segment characters, so per-start work is **O(1)** and there are **~n/4** starts → total **O(n)**. Doubling length should **~double** time (~**2×**), under the **3×** cap. The old `{8,}` pattern could rescan the suffix from every `eyJ` → **inferred** quadratic (matches the in-file comment). | **inferred: yes** — not timed in this session |
| **(2) 200k chars ≤ 50 ms** | ~5×10⁴ bounded attempts vs an unbounded suffix scan on 2×10⁵ chars; isolated `replace` on this regex should stay **well under 50 ms** on typical Node/V8. | **inferred: yes** — no ms sample here |

**Work growth when input doubles:** **inferred** **linear (~2×)**, not quadratic.

**Work on 200k `eyJ-` run:** **inferred** **O(n)** with a **2048** cap per segment trial; **guess** often single-digit ms on Node 20+ for this regex alone—that is **not** a measured result.

### Why MODIFY (not PASS)

The pin requires **running** the pattern and reporting **ms**. Without a runner, posting **PASS** would be an unmeasured JWT timing claim (and `post_verdict` rejects that). The code change **inferred** fixes the documented ReDoS shape; **MODIFY** means: re-run the same Node bench locally or in CI and attach **measured** N / 2N times before MC **PASS**.

### Same diff (out of JWT budget scope)

**inferred:** `scrubAssignments` / split assignment patterns address nested `password=` inside values; no cycle, overflow, or never-expire path seen in this scrubber.

